@anon.1d0b41a8d45d477c3029ec78f9b8b434.1146 = private unnamed_addr constant [1017 x i8] c"function __single\0A    complete -f -c ar -n __fish_use_subcommand -a $argv[1] -d $argv[2] # no dash\0Aend\0A\0A__single d \22Delete modules from the archive.\22\0A__single m \22move members in an archive.\22\0A__single p \22Print the specified members of the archive, to the standard output file.\22\0A__single q \22Quick append; Historically, add the files member... to the end of archive, without checking for replacement.\22\0A__single r \22Insert the files member... into archive (with replacement).\22\0A__single s \22Add an index to the archive, or update it if it already exists.\22\0A__single t \22Display a table listing the contents of archive, or those of the files listed in member.\22\0A__single x \22Extract members (named member) from the archive.\22\0A\0Afunctions -e __single\0A\0A# TODO add mod\0A# A number of modifiers (mod) may immediately follow the p keyletter, to specify variations on an operation's behavior:\0A# add dash\0A# command format\0A# ar [emulation options] [-]{dmpqrstx}[abcDfilMNoOPsSTuvV] [--plugin <name>] [member-name] [count] archive-file file\0A", align 1
