0Acomplete -c tree -s h -d 'Print the size in a more human readable way'\0Acomplete -c tree -l si -d 'Like -h, but use in SI units (powers of 1000)'\0Acomplete -c tree -l du -d 'Compute size of directories by their contents'\0Acomplete -c tree -s D -d 'Print the date of last modification or (-c) status change'\0Acomplete -c tree -l timefmt -x -d 'Print and format time according to the format <f>'\0Acomplete -c tree -s F -d 'Appends \\'/\\', \\'=\\', \\'*\\', \\'@\\', \\'|\\' or \\'>\\' as per ls -F'\0Acomplete -c tree -l inodes -d 'Print inode number of each file'\0Acomplete -c tree -l device -d 'Print device ID number to which each file belongs'\0A\0A## Sorting options\0Acomplete -c tree -s v -d 'Sort files alphanumerically by version'\0Acomplete -c tree -s t -d 'Sort files by last modification time'\0Acomplete -c tree -s c -d 'Sort files by last status change time'\0Acomplete -c tree -s U -d 'Leave files unsorted'\0Acomplete -c tree -s r -d 'Reverse the order of the sort'\0Acomplete -c tree -l dirsfirst -d 'List directories before files (-U disables)'\0Acomplete -c tree -l filesfirst -d 'List files before directories (-U disables)'\0Acomplete -c tree -l sort -d 'Select sort' -xa 'name version size mtime ctime'\0A\0A## Graphics options\0Acomplete -c tree -s i -d 'Don\\'t print indentation lines'\0Acomplete -c tree -s A -d 'Print ANSI lines graphic indentation lines'\0Acomplete -c tree -s S -d 'Print with CP437 (console) graphics indentation lines'\0Acomplete -c tree -s n -d 'Turn colorization off always (-C overrides)'\0Acomplete -c tree -s C -d 'Turn colorization on always'\0A\0A## XML/HTML/JSON options\0Acomplete -c tree -s X -d 'Prints out an XML representation of the tree'\0Acomplete -c tree -s J -d 'Prints out an JSON representation of the tree'\0Acomplete -c tree -s H -r -d 'Prints out HTML format with baseHREF as top directory'\0Acomplete -c tree -s T -r -d 'Replace the default HTML title and H1 header with string'\0Acomplete -c tree -l nolinks -d 'Turn off hyperlinks in HTML output'\0A\0A## Input options\0Acomplete -c tree -l fromfile -r -d 'Reads paths from files (.=stdin)'\0A\0A## Miscellaneous options\0Acomplete -c tree -l version -d 'Print version and exit'\0Acomplete -c tree -l help -d 'Print usage and this help message and exit'\0A", align 1
